        <infoLink name="Rapier Carrier" id="bf7b-a50c-d97d-865a" hidden="false" targetId="e988-89ab-525e-47f3" type="profile"/>
        <infoLink name="Angels of Death" id="3673-6cbd-ab0d-dbde" hidden="false" targetId="01a4-bec8-b573-fde7" type="rule"/>
      </infoLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Space Marine Gunners" id="ff83-3bf3-f035-dbd5" hidden="false">
          <description>When a Rapier Carrier is set up on the battlefield, its Space Marine Gunners are set up in unit coherency with it. From that point onwards the Space Marine Gunners are treated as one unit and the Rapier Carrier as another. The Space Marine Gunners may only be chosen as a target in the Shooting phase if they are the closest visible enemy unit to the firer</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Artillery" id="67f8-5aa1-f731-12c0" hidden="false">
          <description>The Rapier Carrier can only fire its weapon if at least one of the Space Marine Gunners it was deployed with is within 3&quot;. If both of the Space Marine Gunners the Rapier Carrier was depolyed with are slain, the Rapier Carrier is also removed as slain.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
